(text "U24 shares the dedicated QSPI pads with the RP2354B in-package flash die (datasheet Sec 14.3): CLK = QSPI_SCLK,\nDI/IO0 = QSPI_SD0, DO/IO1 = QSPI_SD1, WP/IO2 = QSPI_SD2, HOLD/IO3 = QSPI_SD3. Only the chip select differs -\nFLASH_CS1 comes from GPIO0 (QMI CS1n), pulled up to V3V3_SYS by R35 so the part is deselected before the MCU\ndrives it. QSPI_SS (the internal die) keeps its own strap on the MCU sheet." (at 15 245 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left top)) (uuid cf670b60-a815-5c39-a389-cc25b68e6faf))
(text "J11: DET_A to GND and DET_B to SD_DET with a 10k pull-up, so the input reads low with a card inserted. The\nshield goes to GND. 100 nF + 10 uF + 47 uF sit at the socket (DESIGN_SPEC \"Rails\": SD transients stay on the\nbuck rail). 10k pull-ups on CMD and DAT0-DAT3 are the SD-standard idle bias and also keep DAT3/CD high for\n4-bit mode. VDD = V3V3_SYS." (at 15 268 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left top)) (uuid d7eab09c-1318-5944-a386-64e3e1caa693))
